GOBBY: THE OUTCAST GOBLIN - STORY BRAIN DUMP
MAIN CONCEPT:
- Gobby is a goblin outcast, exiled from his tribe for refusing to embrace their cruelty.
- He wanders into human lands, arriving at the city of Alexandrite, where fantasy creatures are second-class citizens.
- His journey explores racism, slavery, and the blurred morality between humans and non-humans.
- Over time, Gobby transforms from an idealistic outcast into a ruthless warlord.


*Volume 1*
THE FALL OF INNOCENCE
- Gobby, a forest goblin, saves a human princess from two river goblins in the forest, killing one named Bog and maiming the 
   other named Beetle.
- He is nearly executed by the red-haired knight Reihner, who sees all goblins as filth.
- The sorceress remains neutral, simply observing.
- A druid sees Gobby’s actions as a sign of fate and argues for his life.
- The large, emotional knight who protects the princess, hesitates but follows her lead.
- The princess, initially soft-hearted, grows firm in her stance and declares a life debt to Gobby.
- This is unheard of, as fantasy creatures are typically seen as monsters or lesser beings. There is debate how the crowns 
   reputations will hold this
- Gobby, barely conscious, expresses that he understands why humans hate goblins and that it’s okay to put him down.
- He passes out before knowing his fate.
- Gobby comes to in a carriage. Shackled by large cuffs at the wrist with the druid. She healed him and explains destiny to 
   Gobby
- The carriage and hero party with the princess is attacked at the gates with a war party led by a slightly healed Beetle
- Beetle wants revenge for the attack Gobby did on him, His dead brother, and his missed toy (the princess).
- Carriage is attacked and busted in combat. Gobby escapes and frees himself of the shackles.
- Gobby helps out in the fight. Prevents a guard from dying and uses himself as a distraction so a hero can kill Beetle. Breaking 
   the war party will and they retreats
- Now that people saw what Gobby did and now in front of more guards. The princess does a more formal acknowledgement 
   of a life debt to Gobby

SURVIVAL & DISILLUSIONMENT
- Gobby is forced into servitude in the capital, as most goblins are seen as vile and don't have rights yet. Working as an 
   indentured servant in the castle. Stating not being put to death and given work is giving him life.
- This satisfies the powers that are against creature rights and quells the voices that are pro.  
- He witnesses firsthand the cruelty of humans toward fantasy creatures.
- Gobby does see the beauty of what humans make. Sees kinds from an old lady here. A lonely old man shop keeper there. 
   These events are rare though but adds to the internal conflict towards humans.
- in Gobbys indentured servitude to the castle he see and interacts with he princess he saves. They develop a bond and 
    friendship that develops slightly romantic before the princesses tragic end
- Underground battle arenas exist where non-humans fight for entertainment.
- Gobby coaxed or coerce into the under ground fight seen for some time. This is where he learns to fight
- Sorceress and druid find out about Gobby in the under ground fight scene. Teach him the basic of magic for an edge. They
   both take advantage and win some bets. 
- Corruption within the kingdom is rampant, but the king is unaware of its full extent.
- Gobby begins questioning whether coexistence is truly possible.
- Gobbys escape attempt fails, leading to brutal consequences.
- Political strife in kingdom due to the recent minor changes allowing more rights to the creature races of the city state
- The king is a well-intentioned ruler but blind to the corruption beneath him.
- The king is on the side of rights for all but gets to much political push back and threats off civil war if just gives all rights
- The king loves his daughter dearly but is very naïve to the depths mankind will go to get what they want.
- The crown becomes under pressure from all sides. They want a firm stance and laws from the crown.

ALEXANDRIA UNDER SEIGE
- A conspiracy brews
- Something motivates the forest Goblin warlord to mobilize against Alexandria
- The goblin warlord is Gobbys father who exiled him for not being like the rest of his kind. Father thinks he should have ate 
   Gobby
- There are reports in the background of the story leading up till now of an increase in goblin sightings.
- A full fledge Goblin and Hobgoblin army arrives at Alexandria's doorstep what seems overnight somehow. The city is under 
   siege and blocked aid
- Gobby learns of the Warlords name. Already fearing it was his father but in denial. No knowing the truth
- Gobby informs the crown of his connection to the Goblin Warlord. He pleas to speak with his father and barter for peace
- Gobby is sent out. He is quickly captured and sent to his father. They talk. They debate. Gobby is then challenged to fight his 
   father if he wants them to leave. Take his place as Warlord and can command the army
- Gobby loses and is reminded why he is exiled. Branded or scared by the father
- Gobby shammed sneaks back into city and wishes comfort of the princess. 
- Finds her murdered in her chambers where guards are quick to enter and try to arrest Gobby
- Gobby escapes the city after witnessing yet another atrocity and blamed for the murder of the princess

*Volume 2*
EXILE 
- Gobby wonders from place to place. Sometimes accepting of creature places most the time not.
- Excepting or not Gobby usually enters towns unknown or in disguise
- Finds a village that is nothing but a mixture of different "Monsters"
- Is really the idea and perfect spot for Gobby
- The years of trauma and abuse makes where Gobby convinces himself he has to leave the "Monster Village"
- He befriends a female fairy who is a whimsical bossy bratty that can be very caring and down to earth when she opens up.
- Gobby and fairy meet in giant mushroom patch and instantly make a bond
- Gobby and fairy travel for a short time before settling down 
- He and the fairy live in seclusion, trying to find peace away from both humans and goblins and other creatures.

THE SEED OF REVENGE
- A chance encounter with another hero adventuring party looking for a deadly winged female creature
- A group of ‘heroes’ mistake the fairy for a threat and kill her.
- This event breaks Gobby’s faith in humanity even more and also belief structure.
- Gobby hunts down the creature that the heroes were actually after
- He sets out to unite the broken goblin, hob, and ogre tribes in that area
- While trying to unite the tribes he learns there is stories of his deeds of him killing the kings whelp. This sparked honor in his 
   father and respected his wishes and called a temporary with draw. Goblin kind respect Gobby for this.
- He begins forming a unification to stand against the heroes that killed his beloved fairy.
- Uses the unification to draw the heroes out and defeats them. Sacrificing many goblins, hobs, and ogres in the process but 
   wins.



Volume 3
WAR AND TRANSFORMATION
- Gobbys victory calls him to other creatures of the lands to seek his aid. Most calls are for help against cruelty
- Some calls are under the guise of self fulfillment
- Gobby bends his beliefs and helps the creatures that do the same cruelty all in the name of unifying the creatures together 
- Gobby gathers an army of outcasts—creatures who never would have allied under normal circumstances.
- Battles are fought and lost as the creatures begin uniting.
- Gobby becomes more ruthless, justifying his actions as necessary for survival.
- He starts resembling the warlords he once despised.

DOWNWARD SPRIAL
- A series of defeats happen
- Some well established characters are lost
- Gobby becomes more ruthless, justifying his actions as necessary for survival.
- He starts resembling the warlords he once despised.
- A series of victories happen but at what cost.
- Many creatures from Gnomes, centaurs, fairy, goblins, faction of elves join the cause to fight.
- The cause to fight becomes the extinction of all humans

THE END OF MONSTERS
- Majority of world is chaos for humans. Very few cities remain.
- Gobby over confidently sends an all out push to Alexandrite. Where it all began. 
- The final confrontation against the humans leads to mass bloodshed.
- Gobby loses. His army is crushed.
- Most fantasy creatures are killed or forced into hiding.
- Most that go into hiding are hunted down and into extinction
- Gobby, once an idealist, has become exactly what he once swore he’d never be.
- With no more creatures and "monsters" in the world, humans turn to calling their own vile actions for the name of the 
   creatures
- His downfall marks the reason why fantasy creatures no longer exist in the modern world.



*Notes*
THEMES & CHARACTER ARCS:
- **Racism & Oppression** – How systemic oppression warps both the oppressors and the oppressed.
- **Blurred Morality** – No clear good vs. evil. Humans and goblins, fey, beastfolk all commit atrocities.
- **Transformation & Corruption** – Gobby’s descent from idealist to warlord.
- **The Cost of Revenge** – Is vengeance ever justified if it turns you into what you hated?

NOTES & FUTURE IDEAS:
- Possible subplot involving a faction of humans who sympathize with fantasy creatures.
- Gobby’s final act could be leaving behind a legacy that inspires future non-human rebellions.
- Anthology. At least three volumes
